OL,3,ABorrowing surge puts pressure on
OL,4,Achancellor ahead of Budget
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe government borrowed more than
OL,7,Fexpected in August, as persistently
OL,8,Fhigher inflation pushed up overall
OL,9,Fspending.
OL,11,FBorrowing - the difference between tax
OL,12,Freceipts and government spending - was
OL,13,F#18.3bn in August, almost a fifth
OL,14,Fhigher than the year before, the Office
OL,15,Ffor National Statistics (ONS) said.
OL,17,FIt means the government is borrowing
OL,18,Fmore than official forecasters
OL,19,Fexpected, adding to pressure on
OL,20,FChancellor John Healey as he prepares
OL,21,Fto deliver his first Budget on 28
OL,22,FOctober.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
